### What is Collectors.toMap?

Collectors.toMap collects stream elements into a Map by applying a key extractor and a value extractor to each element.

### Why does the two-argument form crash on duplicates?

```java
package com.bank.service;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;
import java.util.function.Function;

public class TradeAggregator {

    // WORKS when keys are unique:
    Map<String, BigDecimal> tradeAmounts = trades.stream()
        .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getTradeId, Trade::getAmount));
    // {TRD-001: 245050, TRD-002: 176000}

    // CRASHES when keys duplicate:
    // Two trades have symbol "RELIANCE" → duplicate key!
    Map<String, BigDecimal> bySymbol = trades.stream()
        .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount));
    // IllegalStateException: Duplicate key RELIANCE
}
```

### How does the merge function resolve duplicates?

```java
// Keep FIRST value (existing wins):
Map<String, BigDecimal> first = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount,
        (existing, incoming) -> existing));

// Keep LAST value (incoming wins):
Map<String, BigDecimal> last = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount,
        (existing, incoming) -> incoming));

// SUM values (aggregate):
Map<String, BigDecimal> total = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount,
        BigDecimal::add));
// RELIANCE: 245050 + 123750 = 368800

// MAX value:
Map<String, BigDecimal> max = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount,
        BigDecimal::max));
```

### How do you control the Map implementation?

```java
// LinkedHashMap: preserves insertion order
Map<String, BigDecimal> ordered = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount,
        BigDecimal::add, LinkedHashMap::new));

// TreeMap: sorts by key alphabetically
Map<String, BigDecimal> sorted = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount,
        BigDecimal::add, TreeMap::new));
```

### How do you build a lookup map?

```java
// Entity ID → Entity
Map<String, Trade> tradeLookup = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getTradeId, Function.identity()));
// Function.identity() = the element itself = t -> t

// With merge (if IDs could duplicate):
Map<String, Trade> safeLookup = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getTradeId, Function.identity(),
        (existing, incoming) -> existing));
```

### What about null values?

```java
// WRONG: toMap does NOT allow null values
Map<String, String> broken = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getTradeId, Trade::getRiskNote));
// If getRiskNote() returns null → NullPointerException!

// CORRECT: filter nulls or provide a default
Map<String, String> safe = trades.stream()
    .filter(t -> t.getRiskNote() != null)
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getTradeId, Trade::getRiskNote));
```

### What are common mistakes?

```java
// WRONG: no merge function in production
Map<String, BigDecimal> risky = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount));
// Works in testing with unique symbols, crashes in production with duplicates!

// CORRECT: always provide merge function when keys might not be unique
Map<String, BigDecimal> safe = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount, BigDecimal::add));
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

- The two-arg toMap is the most common stream-related production bug. Code reviews should flag it.
- For unmodifiable maps: `Collectors.toUnmodifiableMap(key, value, merge)` (Java 10+).
- toMap with merge function and LinkedHashMap::new is the most complete form for production code.

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- What is the default Map type? (HashMap, with no ordering guarantee.)
- Can toMap produce a ConcurrentHashMap? (Yes: `toMap(key, value, merge, ConcurrentHashMap::new)`.)
- What is the merge function signature? (BinaryOperator<V>: takes two values, returns one.)
